# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rizx Player — repository ignore rules
#
# The public repository ships the app itself (Proyecto/), its license/attribution,
# and user-facing documentation (docs/*.md). Internal AI/spec-driven-development
# working material, local IDE/tooling config, build output, and secrets stay out
# of version control.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Editors / IDE / local tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Internal planning & spec material (kept private) ─────────────────────────
# Root planning docs that guide development but are not part of the shipped project.
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md
/ROADMAP.md
/*_STUDY.md
/PROJECT_CONTEXT_*.md
/RAG_KNOWLEDGE_BASE_*.md
/SDD_*.md
/SPEC_REVIEW_*.md
/skills/
/*_docs_specs_package/

# Internal spec-driven-development docs. Public, user-facing docs live directly in
# docs/*.md (tracked). The working specs / ADRs / plans / checklists below are the
# internal design record and stay private.
/docs/specs/
/docs/adr/
/docs/plans/
/docs/checklists/

# ── Android / Gradle build output ────────────────────────────────────────────
build/
.gradle/
.kotlin/
/captures/
.externalNativeBuild/
.cxx/
*.hprof

# ── Local machine config & signing secrets (NEVER commit) ────────────────────
# The build reads RIZX_* values from Gradle properties or the environment. Keep them in
# ~/.gradle/gradle.properties (outside this repository) — never in the tracked gradle.properties.
local.properties
keystore.properties
signing.properties
secrets.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx
*.pem
*.key
*.p8
*.der
# Service-account and platform config that carries project identifiers or upload rights.
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist
service-account*.json
play-publisher*.json
.env
.env.*

# ── Build artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex

# ── Logs, dumps and editor leftovers ─────────────────────────────────────────
# A saved logcat or heap dump can contain session tokens; a .orig from a merge can contain
# whatever the merge was removing.
*.log
*.orig
*.rej
*.bak
*~
*.swp
node_modules/

# ── Bundled plugins ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Plugin archives shipped inside the APK. Deliberately NOT published: a plugin's whole content is a
# pointer to somewhere, and this repository stays a generic plugin host rather than a distributor of
# anybody's index (see docs/adr/0024-community-lossless-source.md). A clone builds an app with no
# bundled plugins and no section for them, which is the intended public shape.
Proyecto/app/src/main/assets/plugins/

# Agent/MCP local tooling config (not part of the published app)
.mcp.json

# Agent tooling and private planning/ops context (never published; see AGENTS.md conventions).
# docs/AGENT_CONTEXT.md carries local machine paths and operational OAuth/artifact detail.
.agents/
skills-lock.json
RIZX_SHAZAM_RECOGNITION_IMPLEMENTATION.md
docs/AGENT_CONTEXT.md
docs/AGENT_CONTEXT_ARCHIVE.md

# Supabase backend (migrations + Edge Functions) is deployment state, applied via MCP/CLI; not published.
supabase/
